  ('guardian-world', 'The Guardian', 'Healthy diet too expensive for one in three people globally, UN report finds', 'https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/jul/21/healthy-diet-too-expensive-for-one-in-three-people-globally-un-report-finds', 'Global hunger declined for the third year in a row in 2025 but experts call for action to bring down costs of fruit, vegetables and dairy as report shows 2.69bn people can’t afford to eat well One in three people cannot afford to eat a healthy diet, a new report has found, prompting calls for urgent action on food affordability. There are 2.69 billion people unable to afford a diverse diet that meets their energy and nutrient needs, and it will take “', '2026-07-21 10:00:42+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('democracynow', 'Democracy Now!', 'Nearly 1,000 Wildfires in Canada Continue to Burn as Trump & Carney Double Down on Fossil Fuels', 'http://www.democracynow.org/2026/7/20/canada_wildfires', 'Millions of people across North America have experienced hazardous air pollution this month as nearly a thousand active wildfires continue to rage in Canada. In addition to releasing hazardous chemicals and smoke darkening skies across the continent, the fires in Canada have also disproportionately impacted Indigenous communities, forcing thousands to evacuate their homes. Republican politicians have been loath to acknowledge the role of the climate crisis in making extreme weather events like t', '2026-07-20 12:51:52+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('democracynow', 'Democracy Now!', 'Texas Rep. Al Green Accuses Trump Admin of Attempting to Cover Up ICE Killings', 'http://www.democracynow.org/2026/7/20/lorenzo_salgado_araujo', 'As calls mount for accountability over the ICE killing of Lorenzo Salgado Araujo in Houston, we speak with Democratic Congressmember Al Green, who represents Texas’s 9th Congressional District. He demands an independent investigation into the shooting to stop “an attempt to cover up” the killing by the Trump administration. Democratic lawmakers led by the Congressional Hispanic Caucus will hold a public hearin', '2026-07-20 12:40:40+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('democracynow', 'Democracy Now!', '"Justice for Lorenzo": Houston Community Demands Accountability After ICE Killing of Mexican Father', 'http://www.democracynow.org/2026/7/20/report_from_houston', 'Houston community members continue to demand justice for Lorenzo Salgado Araujo, the 52-year-old Mexican father who was shot and killed by an ICE agent July 7. He had lived in the United States for nearly 35 years and had three U.S. citizen children. The ICE agents involved in his killing have not been identified, and it’s unclear whether they remain on active duty. For more on the community', '2026-07-20 12:23:56+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('democracynow', 'Democracy Now!', 'U.S. Escalates War on Iran, Targeting Civilian Infrastructure as 3 U.S. Soldiers Are Killed', 'http://www.democracynow.org/2026/7/20/iran_update', 'The United States is expanding its attacks on Iran after three U.S. soldiers were killed over the weekend, the first U.S. fatalities in the conflict since March. Two U.S. service members were killed in an Iranian attack on a base in Jordan, and a third soldier was killed in northern Iraq during a “controlled detonation” of a downed Iranian drone. The United States has now bombed Iran for nine consecutive nights, and Iran has retaliated by striking U.S. allies across the Persi', '2026-07-20 12:12:30+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
