  ('ballotpedia', 'Ballotpedia', 'State government responses to the Supreme Court ruling in Louisiana v. Callais', 'https://ballotpedia.org/State_government_responses_to_the_Supreme_Court_ruling_in_Louisiana_v._Callais', 'Ballotpedia living tracker (last updated June 4, 2026): post-Callais state responses — election date and filing deadline changes (Alabama''s August 11 special congressional primary; Louisiana''s HB 842 moving U.S. House races to November 3), post-Callais redistricting efforts in Alabama, Louisiana, South Carolina, and Tennessee, litigation affected by the ruling, and noteworthy 2026 legislation. Reference/tracker page; is_digest candidate.', '2026-06-04 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('ballotpedia', 'Ballotpedia', 'Redistricting in Louisiana ahead of the 2026 elections', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Redistricting_in_Louisiana_ahead_of_the_2026_elections', 'Ballotpedia living tracker of Louisiana''s mid-decade redistricting: the Callais litigation line from the January 2024 lawsuit through the April 29, 2026 ruling, the timeline of map proposals and approvals culminating in Gov. Landry signing the new congressional map on May 29, 2026, and national context (ten states with new maps, net +10 Republican). Reference/tracker page; is_digest candidate.', '2026-06-01 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('nola-com-the-advocate', 'NOLA.com / The Advocate', 'Gov. Jeff Landry signs Louisiana''s new congressional map after fierce political battles', 'https://www.nola.com/news/politics/legislature/jeff-landry-signs-louisiana-redistricting-bill-congress/article_770ef156-f8b0-442d-9c22-d555b2ff1466.html', 'NOLA.com/The Advocate: Gov. Jeff Landry signs Louisiana''s new congressional map into law after weeks of fierce political battle triggered by the Callais ruling, finalizing the SB 121 remap that eliminates one majority-Black district. (Headline-derived summary: page retrieval failed at fetch time.)', '2026-05-29 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('league-of-women-voters', 'League of Women Voters', 'SCOTUS''s Final Blow Dismantling the Voting Rights Act', 'https://www.lwv.org/blog/scotuss-final-blow-dismantling-voting-rights-act', 'LWV blog analysis: Callais effectively eliminated Section 2 by rewriting vote-dilution rules so plaintiffs cannot succeed; 191 state legislative seats and 19 congressional seats held from majority-Black districts are at risk; the League has already challenged Florida''s new map and the Louisiana primary cancellation.', '2026-05-21 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('brennan-center', 'Brennan Center', 'Congress Must Respond to Callais', 'https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/congress-must-respond-callais', 'Brennan Center research report (Weiser, Sweren-Becker): Callais is the Roberts Court''s third and gravest blow to the VRA; Congress has constitutional authority to respond and should ban partisan gerrymandering and mid-decade redistricting, enact an enforceable right to vote with national standards, and adopt Supreme Court term limits.', '2026-05-20 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('campaign-legal-center', 'Campaign Legal Center', 'Redistricting 101 and the Fight for Fair Representation After Callais', 'https://campaignlegal.org/sites/default/files/2026-05/Redistricting%20101%20and%20the%20Fight%20for%20Fair%20Representation%20After%20Callais.pdf', 'Campaign Legal Center explainer (PDF): how Callais changed Section 2 analysis — challengers must now show legislators intended to discriminate, not merely discriminatory impact; what the ruling means for voters in Florida, Louisiana, Tennessee and beyond, and what protections remain. (Date is the manifest''s mid-month placeholder.)', '2026-05-15 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('louisiana-illuminator', 'Louisiana Illuminator', 'Louisiana Senate committee drops one of two majority-Black districts in advancing map', 'https://lailluminator.com/2026/05/13/louisiana-senate-committee-drops-one-of-two-majority-black-districts-in-advancing-map/', 'Louisiana Illuminator: in a nearly 10-hour overnight hearing, the Senate and Governmental Affairs Committee approved SB 121 (Morris) 4-3 on party lines, advancing a map that eliminates the majority-Black 6th district and would give Republicans five of six House seats; SB 407 rejected.', '2026-05-13 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('wafb', 'WAFB', 'Cleo Fields vows to fight Louisiana redistricting plan as map advances', 'https://www.wafb.com/2026/05/13/cleo-fields-vows-fight-louisiana-redistricting-plan-map-advances/', 'WAFB: Rep. Cleo Fields vows to fight for fair representation as SB 121 moves to the full Senate; the report also notes Sen. Jay Morris said he and his staff received death threats after the contentious overnight committee hearing on the Callais-triggered remap.', '2026-05-13 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('honest-elections-project-alec', 'Honest Elections Project / ALEC', 'Louisiana v. Callais and the Future of Redistricting', 'https://alec.org/article/louisiana-v-callais-and-the-future-of-redistricting/', 'ALEC task-force interview with HEP''s Jason Snead and ARP''s Adam Kincaid: Callais is ''an opportunity to reset redistricting'' around constitutional standards; advises map-drawers to separate race from politics, document criteria, and consider drawing maps without racial data. Approving commentary (hosted on alec.org).', '2026-05-12 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('public-interest-legal-foundation', 'Public Interest Legal Foundation', 'Lawsuit: Illinois Violates Fifteenth Amendment, Voting Rights Act After Callais Decision', 'https://publicinterestlegal.org/press/lawsuit-illinois-violates-fifteenth-amendment-voting-rights-act-after-callais-decision/', 'PILF press release: the first lawsuit filed after Callais, challenging the Illinois Voting Rights Act of 2011 on behalf of Jeanne Ives; J. Christian Adams: ''States may not use race to allocate power.'' Approving use of the ruling — PILF argues Callais makes explicit racial redistricting criteria unconstitutional.', '2026-05-11 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('votebeat', 'Votebeat', 'Two reminders that the rules of the 2026 election are still in flux', 'https://www.votebeat.org/national/2026/05/11/louisiana-alabama-tennessee-redistricting-trump-executive-order-2026-election/', 'Votebeat national analysis: with under six months to the general election, last-minute redistricting after Callais is forcing primaries to be rescheduled and confusing voters in Louisiana, Alabama, and Tennessee, alongside a Trump executive order — two signs the 2026 rules are still moving.', '2026-05-11 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('league-of-women-voters-common-cause-lulac', 'League of Women Voters / Common Cause / LULAC', 'Voting Rights Groups Sue to Stop Florida Congressional Map', 'https://www.lwv.org/newsroom/press-releases/voting-rights-groups-sue-stop-florida-congressional-map', 'Joint press release: LWV of Florida, Common Cause, and LULAC (represented by SPLC, SCSJ, and Democracy Defenders Fund) sued in Leon County circuit court to stop Florida''s new congressional map hours after DeSantis signed it, arguing it violates the Fair Districts Amendments; the release explicitly frames the suit as a response to the Callais decision.', '2026-05-05 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
  ('reuters', 'Reuters', 'How redistricting and the Supreme Court have cut voters out of US House races', 'https://billingsgazette.com/news/nation-world/government-politics/article_fed5f073-5cad-5c66-b4da-d1065b9196bc.html', 'Reuters analysis by Joseph Ax (syndicated copy): only 32 of 435 House seats are competitive, fewest at this stage since at least 2008; the Callais ruling amid the mid-decade gerrymandering war is expected to shrink competition further as Republican-led states target majority-Black and majority-Latino districts — ''no guardrails,'' per Justin Levitt. (Owner-approved substitute for the unlocated Reuters day-of piece.)', '2026-05-03 00:00:00+00', 'Read-only reference import: public source metadata only. No original body text, embeddings, entities, claims, or relationship data were copied.', '[]'::jsonb, false, false, false, 'v2-original-reference-news-2026-08-19', 'active', 'Copied only from the original platform’s public article metadata in a read-only reference pass; source URL retained for verification. No original database relationship or private metadata was imported.'),
